{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Rice Cookout"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "I Will"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The First Conditional vs. The Second Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You use the first conditional to talk about real situations in the the present of future.</p><p>You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "First conditional form:<br/><span class=\"italic\">If</span> + Simple Present verb, + <span class=\"italic\">will</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\">If you come over, I'll help you with that.</span><br/>(you can come over)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Second conditional form:<br/><span class=\"italic\">If</span> + Simple Past verb,    + <span class=\"italic\">would</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\">If you had time, I would help you with that.</span> <br/>(I don't think or I know you don't have time)"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">First Conditional <br/>(Cause and Effect)</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Second Conditional <br/>(Hypothetical Situations)</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>If you overcook food it will be less exciting to eat.</p><p>If we warm up our food again, won't it be overcooked?</p><p>If you try out a dish, slice up the vegetables nice and thick so they'll cook slower.</p></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>If you learned to cook more dishes, you wouldn't always be hungry.</p><p>If we both learned a bit more, Peter, we could whip up some food together.</p><p>If we made something from Vanessa's blog we could take a picture and post it.</p></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember to use a comma (,) after the <span class=\"italic\">IF</span> clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (<span class=\"italic\">I would</span> = <span class=\"italic\">I'd</span>)."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future with <span class=\"italic\">Will</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Going to</span>, the Present Simple"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use three different tenses to talk about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about things that are scheduled, like programs, classes, busses or trains, you use the Present Simple tense."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Deciding Now</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>I'll try that.</p><p>They'll still be crunchy!</p></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Intentions</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>You guys are actually going to do up your own food! </p><p>I'm going to cook them less? </p></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Schedules</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>It comes on in the early evening right?</p><p>It starts again next weekend and plays from 1:00 to 3:00. </p></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to whip up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make quickly and easily"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How did you whip up that dessert so quickly?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words to review."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to do up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to create; package; put together"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You could have someone else do up your meal!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to slice up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cut with a sharp knife"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Use this disc to slice up the vegetables with the food processor."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to post"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put on a website"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm going to post these pictures on my website."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to try out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to experiment with; to test"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm trying out different dishes this weekend."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to warm up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make hotter"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This one can warm up cold food too!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "overcooked"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "cooked too much"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: No more overcooked vegetables!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob11aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le18ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Decide on some activities you want to do on the weekend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down a plan of the activities you would like to do and when. (Use simple present, e.g. <span class=\"italic\">On Saturday, I meet Sarah at 10.</span>)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tell someone about your plans."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I choose some activities to do on the weekend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a plan for the weekend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about my plans."}]}], "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about future actions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about cause and effects and hypothetical situations."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about cooking and social activities."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How often do you have dinner with friends?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you stay in or go out for dinner?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " If you stay in, do you cook together or do you take turns making a meal?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type"